interface Signalled is

   --  Sent by the kernel to a process that has signal bits set (ADR
   --  0006, #708), the next time it receives, after the restore notice
   --  and before any other message. Bits is every bit that is set, and
   --  they are cleared. Bits 8 to 31 are the process's own, set through
   --  the signal caps it gave out. Rose.Server calls the handler that the
   --  process registered for each bit.

   procedure Signal (Bits : Word_32);

end Signalled;
